# Entity Modules

## Folder layout

Each module is `src/Entities/<PascalName>/`:

```
Contatos.php                 # public entity class
Enum/<Name>.php              # backed enums for this resource
Schema/<Operation>/*.php     # params and response classes for one operation
Schema/@shared/*.php         # variants shared by several operations of this module
__tests__/                   # colocated PHPUnit specs and JSON fixtures
```

Reference modules: `src/Entities/Contatos/`, `src/Entities/CamposCustomizados/`, `src/Entities/Produtos/`, `src/Entities/Empresas/`.

## Base class

Every entity extends `BaseEntity` (`src/Entities/@shared/BaseEntity.php`) and receives `IBlingRepository` through the constructor. The repository is available as `$this->repository`.

## Class conventions

- The class name matches the folder: `Contatos` in `src/Entities/Contatos/Contatos.php`.
- The class is a concrete, non-readonly subclass of `BaseEntity`.
- The class docblock is one Portuguese line plus `@see` to the Bling resource section.
- Methods are `public` and synchronous.
- A method builds `new RequestOptions(...)`, calls one repository verb, and returns `*Response::fromResponse($response)`.
- The PHP return type is that response class, or `null` when `fromResponse` returns `null`.

## Method names

| Method | Repository call | Reference |
|--------|-----------------|-----------|
| `get` | `index` | `src/Entities/Contatos/Contatos.php` |
| `find` | `show` | `src/Entities/Contatos/Contatos.php` |
| `create` | `store` | `src/Entities/CamposCustomizados/CamposCustomizados.php` |
| `update` | `replace` for PUT, `update` for PATCH | `Contatos::update` uses `replace` |
| `delete` | `destroy` | `src/Entities/Contatos/Contatos.php` |
| `changeSituation` | verb of the Bling operation | `CamposCustomizados::changeSituation` uses `update` |

Name a non-CRUD action after the Bling action in English: `send`, `download`, `postStock`, `reverseAccounts`, `generateNfe`, `getModules`. POST actions call `store` (`Nfes::postStock` → `nfe/{id}/lancar-estoque`).

## Endpoint and parameter patterns

- Endpoint strings are double-quoted, kebab-case, and include every path id: `"contatos/$idContato"`, `"contatos/$idContato/tipos"`, `"contas/pagar/$idContaPagar"`.
- Collection and filter calls take `*Params|array $params` when the operation needs it, or `*Params|array|null $params = null` when the filter is optional, and pass `$params` through as `queryParams`. The array uses the same keys the Params object serializes. See `Produtos::deleteMany` and `Contatos::get`.
- `create` and other JSON writes take `array $body` and pass it as `body`.
- Date filters are converted inside the `*Params` constructor with `prepareStringOrDateParam` (`Contatos\Schema\Get\GetParams`).
- An operation with an empty success body uses a response class whose `fromResponse` returns `null`. The entity method's return type is `null` (`Contatos::delete`).
- Extra headers go on `RequestOptions` as `headers: ['x-bling-homologacao' => $hash]` (`Homologacao`).

## Shared types

Import `UF`, `TipoPessoa`, and `Genero` from `Entities\Shared\Enum` when the Bling field uses those exact cases. A `Situacao` enum lives in the module's `Enum/` folder (`Contatos\Enum\Situacao`, `Produtos\Enum\Situacao`, `CamposCustomizados\Enum\Situacao`).

Use `Entities\Shared\DTO\Schema\Id` when the nested JSON object is only `{ "id": <int> }`.
